COMMIT 94b6d02198607f3d36f8e9d0e5713ff215736219
fix(core): one producer that will not close no longer strands the others

The close loop caught RuntimeException around p.close(), so an Error from one producer abandoned the
loop itself: every producer after it was never asked to close and never joined settled, leaking the
sockets, pools and file handles of producers nothing ever touched. Widened to Throwable, which hands
a synchronous throw to the recover that already defines the right shutdown behaviour - log at WARNING
naming the flow and the producer, carry on to the next. A multicatch was refused for the reason
FIX-136 recorded, and the measurement here says the same (M2 below): it drops the sneaky checked
throwable an interrupted await produces.

The reviewer found the defect worse than the packet stated, in two ways worth keeping. Before the fix
the Error escaped after `asked` was set true and before `closed` completed, so a SECOND close() hung
for good. And at FlowBuilder:464, where closeAll sits in a finally with its return value discarded,
the escaping Error REPLACED the build's own exception - FIX-140's shape a third time. It checked the
three callers and grepped for a fatal-Error policy (UncaughtExceptionHandler, VirtualMachineError,
halt), finding none on this path, so nothing relied on the escape.

The class javadoc is rewritten beyond the packet, because it had documented the defect as if it were
intended: "an Error is not caught: it propagates... the close never completes". The provenance was
checked before accepting that rewrite - nothing in docs/DECISIONS.md mentions Producers and nothing
in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md covers close semantics, so the sentence described the code rather than
recording an intent. Had a decision backed it, this task would have needed a finding first.

Checks: VERIFIED_PASS integrated on 0adcbed - ProducersCloseTest 19/0/0/0, flottila-core 555/0/0/0,
and the four classes the last four tasks touched run together 124/0/0/0
(agent/work/FIX-141-integrated.log). All five mutants killed, cmp clean after each, every section
opening with a diff of the backup against the mutated file (agent/work/FIX-141-mutants.log): the
catch narrowed back to RuntimeException 13 failures; the D-104 multicatch 6; failedFuture(thrown) to
succeededFuture() 7; the WARNING losing its attached throwable 3; Future.all(settled).mapEmpty() to
succeededFuture() 3.

Also in this commit, from the preceding tasks: FIX-145, the interrupt flag this widened catch now
makes reachable, split out of the review rather than left inside it; FIX-146, six PROGRESS entries
that exist only in docs/PROGRESS.md and never reached the journal docs/WORKFLOW.md:48 names; and the
NOTES lesson that cost the most here - a lane hand-off diff made with `git diff` silently omits
untracked files, so this task's diff carried the production fix with no test and would have gone
green because nothing tested it. Caught by git status --porcelain in the lane before applying.

